[
  {
    "id": "tab_mcp23008_demo",
    "type": "tab",
    "label": "MCP23008 Demo",
    "info": "Output control and input polling on the MCP23008 (I²C) / MCP23S08 (SPI) 8-bit IO expander.\n\nHardware:\n- GP0–GP3: four LEDs (anode through 220 Ω, cathode to GND; active-high)\n- GP4–GP7: push buttons to GND (internal pull-ups enabled in the driver's Full configuration)\n\nHow it works:\n1. An Inject node every 200 ms feeds a Function node that writes a rotating one-hot pattern to the LEDs (GP0→GP3), one pin at a time.\n2. A second Inject node reads the full 8-bit port every second; a Function node formats the hex value for a Debug node.\n3. A third Inject node reads GP4 (a button input); a Debug node shows the 0/1 level.\n\nSwitch the node's transport between I²C and SPI in its config panel; the flow is otherwise identical.\n\nTo observe: watch the LEDs chase and press the buttons; the port value changes in the debug sidebar."
  },
  {
    "id": "inj_rotate",
    "type": "inject",
    "z": "tab_mcp23008_demo",
    "name": "Rotate 200ms",
    "repeat": "0.2",
    "payload": "",
    "payloadType": "date",
    "topic": "",
    "once": false,
    "x": 120,
    "y": 60,
    "wires": [
      [
        "fn_rotate"
      ]
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "fn_rotate",
    "type": "function",
    "z": "tab_mcp23008_demo",
    "name": "One-hot pattern",
    "func": "const i = Math.floor(Date.now() / 200) % 4;\nconst prev = (i + 3) % 4;\nreturn [[{ payload: { pin: prev, value: 0 } }, { payload: { pin: i, value: 1 } }]];",
    "outputs": 1,
    "noerr": 0,
    "x": 330,
    "y": 60,
    "wires": [
      [
        "mcp_write"
      ]
    ]
  },
